n English, flat. Literacy (+30%) is Literacy: Native Language. Pilot: Helicopter is Helicopter and Pilot: Jet Fighter is Military: Jet Fighters; Pilot: Robots and Powered Armor is Robots & Power Armor at its catalog base, no bonus printed; Pilot: Hover Craft is Hover Craft (ground). Read Sensory Equipment is Sensory Equipment; General Athletics is Athletics (general). The floor of two Pilot or Pilot Related skills is stored as a minimum. No horsemanship: City troops are not trained to ride (printed 157). Cowboy, Espionage, Rogue and Wilderness: None are honoured by leaving the categories out. || EQUIPMENT not stored as rows: the padded M.D.C. flight suit (12 M.D.C.) and helmet (35 M.D.C.), which also insulates against extreme cold and acts as a wet-suit, the flight jacket, the weapons locked in the aircraft (2-6 hand grenades, an energy rifle and/or a shotgun or other weapon) and the optional light suit of body armor are in GM Notes. Aircraft, the VR robot helicopter and power armor are vehicles, named in GM Notes. || MONEY: starts with 2D4x$1000 in personal savings; the monthly salary of $3000, +$200 per level, with room and board and medical treatment, is in GM Notes. || NOT STORED: the Door-Gunner (an Air Force Grunt with infantry skills and heavy weapons, no piloting skills) is an NPC note in GM Notes."
