## Lore

Aerojock is the nickname for the pilots of the two Tech-Cities'' Air Forces.
Both forces are well equipped and give Perth and Melbourne a great advantage
in speed, tactics and firepower over anything in the Outback. Their pilots
are well trained, eager and daring; they fly air assault, air support and
transport, and are kept busy with patrols and missions into the Gap, from
diplomatic flights to punitive strikes.

Melbourne''s Air Force is the more aggressive, seasoned and far-reaching of
the two, and its men and women are hawkish in defense of their city and
contemptuous of wilderness folk and nonhumans.

## GM Notes

The Military O.C.C.s introduction on printed 121 says City troops are less
seasoned than those of the Coalition, Triax or Russia (most infantry are 2nd
or 3rd level), have few specialized troops, and use human mutants and
Phreakers where others use mutant animals. The City list on printed 105 says
a City character met outside the walls is an agent, an exile, a criminal, a
rebel or a truant, unless the whole group is a City team on assignment.

Choose the city: a Perth pilot has Helicopter at +20% and Jet Fighter at
+10%; a Melbourne pilot has +15% and +20%, and adds a further 5% to any
flying vehicle taken as a related Pilot skill (the sheet adds 10%).

Kit beyond what the sheet lists (printed 122): a padded M.D.C. flight suit
(12 M.D.C., no movement penalties) and helmet (35 M.D.C.) that insulate
against extreme cold and act as a wet-suit; a flight jacket; optionally a
light suit of body armor. Further weapons are locked down in the aircraft and
may include 2-6 hand grenades, an energy rifle and/or a shotgun or other
weapon. The Aerojock is authorized to use power armor and has access to any
flying vehicle, including the VR robot helicopter, power armor and all types
of aircraft.

Helicopter crews include Door-Gunners, Air Force Grunts with infantry skills
and heavy weapons, often in heavy armor, who have no piloting skills.

Pay: $3000 a month, +$200 per level of experience, with room and board, paid
medical treatment and access to military facilities. Quarters are a
dormitory-style apartment at the Air Force barracks shared with three other
pilots, with simulators and testing grounds on the base.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'aerojock');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'aerojock';

